WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.389
- Good morning, Believe Nation!

00:00:01.389 --> 00:00:02.572
Today's message is

00:00:02.572 --> 00:00:04.808
Don't Stop Working.

00:00:04.808 --> 00:00:06.574
Over to you, Bill Burr.

00:00:06.574 --> 00:00:08.672
(rooster crowing)

00:00:08.672 --> 00:00:11.593
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.593 --> 00:00:14.311
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:00:14.311 --> 00:00:18.516
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:18.516 --> 00:00:20.241
- I enjoy annoying people.

00:00:20.241 --> 00:00:21.550
- I enjoy annoying people.

00:00:21.550 --> 00:00:22.426
I don't know why.

00:00:22.426 --> 00:00:24.395
Not like the whole crowd, obviously,

00:00:24.395 --> 00:00:25.544
'cause then I'd be bombing.

00:00:25.544 --> 00:00:28.537
But there's a segment that's
when I'm having the most fun.

00:00:28.537 --> 00:00:31.402
When 80% of the crowd is loving it

00:00:31.402 --> 00:00:34.763
and then there's that 20% just going,

00:00:34.763 --> 00:00:35.964
just looking around like,

00:00:35.964 --> 00:00:38.129
"How are you laughing at this?"

00:00:38.129 --> 00:00:39.155
People don't notice.

00:00:39.155 --> 00:00:42.209
Sometimes I can see them
and if I can figure out

00:00:42.209 --> 00:00:43.380
what they're reacting to,

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:46.654
it becomes a game to see if
I can get them to yell at me

00:00:46.654 --> 00:00:49.071
or get up and start to leave.

00:00:49.968 --> 00:00:51.894
Other than that, 'cause there's a danger

00:00:51.894 --> 00:00:55.407
once you put together an hour that works.

00:00:55.407 --> 00:00:57.490
You can just stop working

00:00:58.360 --> 00:00:59.372
and just joke.

00:00:59.372 --> 00:01:02.262
I'll just show up, I can drink all night.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:03.811
I'll walk my way through the radio.

00:01:03.811 --> 00:01:05.789
And I just keep doing this
hour that I have memorized

00:01:05.789 --> 00:01:07.329
and I'll be thinking about doing my taxes

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:09.156
as I'm doing my jokes.

00:01:09.156 --> 00:01:12.944
But then what happens is everybody
else catches up with you.

00:01:12.944 --> 00:01:13.830
And the next thing you know,

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:15.130
you're that guy onstage going

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:17.026
"What's up with the Carter administration?

00:01:17.026 --> 00:01:18.381
"This is crazy."

00:01:18.381 --> 00:01:19.669
And you become that guy.

00:01:19.669 --> 00:01:22.448
- Too many entrepreneurs get
bored of their businesses

00:01:22.448 --> 00:01:23.498
and they fail.

00:01:23.498 --> 00:01:26.142
Too many entrepreneurs let the success

00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:28.347
any success that they had in the past

00:01:28.347 --> 00:01:31.201
be chains from them achieving more.

00:01:31.201 --> 00:01:32.791
It happens so often.

00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:34.391
It's crazy how much this happens.

00:01:34.391 --> 00:01:36.550
At the start of being an entrepreneur

00:01:36.550 --> 00:01:38.127
we leave our jobs.

00:01:38.127 --> 00:01:38.960
We leave what most people are doing

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:41.291
We leave what most people are doing

00:01:41.291 --> 00:01:42.909
to go off and do our own thing.

00:01:42.909 --> 00:01:44.287
To be crazy, to be wild,

00:01:44.287 --> 00:01:45.331
to have our own business.

00:01:45.331 --> 00:01:47.050
Set our own rules, be our own boss.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.393
This is how we start off.

00:01:48.393 --> 00:01:50.333
And then you start to get some customers,

00:01:50.333 --> 00:01:51.735
then you start to make
a little bit of money,

00:01:51.735 --> 00:01:52.681
maybe not huge money.

00:01:52.681 --> 00:01:54.180
Maybe you have made huge money.

00:01:54.180 --> 00:01:55.542
But you start to make
a little bit of money.

00:01:55.542 --> 00:01:58.066
And what happens so often
to so many entrepreneurs

00:01:58.066 --> 00:02:00.188
And what happens so often
to so many entrepreneurs

00:02:00.188 --> 00:02:02.420
is once you start making a little bit

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:04.590
once you find the thing that
you've made some money on

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:07.063
then that's all you do.

00:02:07.063 --> 00:02:08.918
And you stop innovating

00:02:08.918 --> 00:02:11.157
and you stop growing
and you stop building.

00:02:11.157 --> 00:02:13.295
And you just focus on this one thing.

00:02:13.295 --> 00:02:15.926
And that is death for an entrepreneur

00:02:15.926 --> 00:02:18.098
because we love creating new stuff.

00:02:18.098 --> 00:02:19.573
We love exploring.

00:02:19.573 --> 00:02:21.385
We love trying out new things.

00:02:21.385 --> 00:02:25.105
And as you grow and you evolve
and change as a human being

00:02:25.105 --> 00:02:26.381
what you need to do

00:02:26.381 --> 00:02:28.699
is bring that to your business.

00:02:28.699 --> 00:02:32.074
Where too many entrepreneurs
get bored of their companies

00:02:32.074 --> 00:02:33.804
because at the start they love it

00:02:33.804 --> 00:02:35.365
'cause it's a reflection of who they are,

00:02:35.365 --> 00:02:36.478
what they want to do.

00:02:36.478 --> 00:02:39.348
And then as they start building it

00:02:39.348 --> 00:02:41.570
they grow and evolve as a human being

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:43.169
but they don't grow and
evolve their business.

00:02:43.169 --> 00:02:45.017
Their businesses are stuck

00:02:45.017 --> 00:02:47.243
doing what they wanted to
do a couple of years ago.

00:02:47.243 --> 00:02:49.680
What Evan loves doing five years ago

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.614
is not the same thing as
what Evan loves doing now.

00:02:52.614 --> 00:02:55.549
And so as I build and
grow as a human being

00:02:55.549 --> 00:02:57.486
I bring that to my business.

00:02:57.486 --> 00:02:59.314
I try new things.

00:02:59.314 --> 00:03:01.130
I like to explore.

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:03.480
And if you find yourself
really getting bored

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:04.945
then what you need to do is

00:03:04.945 --> 00:03:08.041
pass on some of that
business to somebody else.

00:03:08.041 --> 00:03:11.115
What I try to do in my company
is I build up a business

00:03:11.115 --> 00:03:14.422
to the point where I can either
hand it off to somebody else

00:03:14.422 --> 00:03:15.776
or I drop it.

00:03:15.776 --> 00:03:18.455
Most projects that I start
by the way, don't work.

00:03:18.455 --> 00:03:20.869
Most of the new things that
I've put out don't work.

00:03:20.869 --> 00:03:23.315
Most of the new series we've
created for the YouTube channel

00:03:23.315 --> 00:03:24.200
they don't work.

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:27.251
We've cut more series
for this YouTube channel

00:03:27.251 --> 00:03:30.625
than most people ever create
'cause it didn't work.

00:03:30.625 --> 00:03:32.353
A combination of maybe I'm not

00:03:32.353 --> 00:03:33.774
as passionate about it anymore

00:03:33.774 --> 00:03:34.877
and you guys didn't like it either.

00:03:34.877 --> 00:03:36.973
So we dropped it.

00:03:36.973 --> 00:03:39.125
That's okay, that's good.

00:03:39.125 --> 00:03:41.653
And so most of the things
that I tried to start,

00:03:41.653 --> 00:03:44.169
I'll put my own energy and effort into.

00:03:44.169 --> 00:03:45.086
Just me.

00:03:45.086 --> 00:03:47.149
When I started a YouTube
channel, it was just me.

00:03:47.149 --> 00:03:48.746
It was just me.

00:03:48.746 --> 00:03:50.698
And I had no lights and no microphone

00:03:50.698 --> 00:03:51.877
and a really bad camera.

00:03:51.877 --> 00:03:52.873
It was just me.

00:03:52.873 --> 00:03:53.891
And I built it to the point

00:03:53.891 --> 00:03:56.392
where I was able to make
some money off of it.

00:03:56.392 --> 00:03:58.661
And then I hired somebody and
then I hired another person,

00:03:58.661 --> 00:03:59.520
I hired another person.

00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:00.784
Built up a team.

00:04:00.784 --> 00:04:02.820
But most projects for me
don't even go that way.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:04.097
Most projects, I try build it up

00:04:04.097 --> 00:04:05.947
and it doesn't get
anywhere and so I drop it.

00:04:05.947 --> 00:04:07.308
Move on to something else.

00:04:07.308 --> 00:04:09.679
But that experimentation is key.

00:04:09.679 --> 00:04:11.466
You can't stop working.

00:04:11.466 --> 00:04:12.752
You can't stop building.

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:15.313
You can't stop evolving in your company.

00:04:15.313 --> 00:04:17.518
If you are bored right now.

00:04:17.518 --> 00:04:19.276
Most entrepreneurs look to

00:04:19.276 --> 00:04:20.590
I need to sell this business

00:04:20.590 --> 00:04:21.869
and go do something else.

00:04:21.869 --> 00:04:23.980
It's because you've let
it get so far apart.

00:04:23.980 --> 00:04:26.161
The person that you were
when you started the business

00:04:26.161 --> 00:04:27.994
and the person that you've now become

00:04:27.994 --> 00:04:29.933
and you haven't brought
your business with you.

00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:31.078
You've gotten so far apart

00:04:31.078 --> 00:04:33.499
that you're ready to leave
it and do something else.

00:04:33.499 --> 00:04:36.908
Find a way to inject the
new self into your business

00:04:36.908 --> 00:04:39.992
and make it catch up with you constantly.

00:04:39.992 --> 00:04:41.818
And if there are things
that you don't enjoy anymore

00:04:41.818 --> 00:04:43.148
and you don't want to do.

00:04:43.148 --> 00:04:44.273
But still add a lot of value

00:04:44.273 --> 00:04:45.106
and still make money, great.

00:04:45.106 --> 00:04:49.348
Hire somebody on your team
who loves doing that work.

00:04:49.348 --> 00:04:50.860
And give it to them.

00:04:50.860 --> 00:04:52.562
And if you can't afford
to hire somebody to do it.

00:04:52.562 --> 00:04:53.680
Then stop it.

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:57.301
Kill that project 'cause it's
not financially worth it.

00:04:57.301 --> 00:04:59.801
If you're doing projects that
is not making enough money

00:04:59.801 --> 00:05:01.205
to hire somebody else to do

00:05:01.205 --> 00:05:03.073
and you don't want to do it anymore,

00:05:03.073 --> 00:05:04.313
then just drop it.

00:05:04.313 --> 00:05:06.602
And start working on
the work that you love

00:05:06.602 --> 00:05:08.342
'cause that's where you're
going to come alive.

00:05:08.342 --> 00:05:09.848
That's where you're going to create magic.

00:05:09.848 --> 00:05:11.955
You need to evolve with your business.

00:05:11.955 --> 00:05:13.908
Look at a great band like The Beatles.

00:05:13.908 --> 00:05:15.624
Maybe the greatest band of all time.

00:05:15.624 --> 00:05:18.315
Their first album was not the
same as their second album

00:05:18.315 --> 00:05:19.624
was not the same as their third album.

00:05:19.624 --> 00:05:21.110
The reason why they had
so much sustainability

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:23.200
was because they evolved their business

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.809
as they evolved as human beings.

00:05:24.809 --> 00:05:28.928
If they stuck to just doing
the same album every time

00:05:28.928 --> 00:05:31.752
they would be a one-album wonder.

00:05:31.752 --> 00:05:33.605
And nobody would pay
attention to them anymore.

00:05:33.605 --> 00:05:37.210
But as they grew and as they evolved.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:40.637
Their business grew and
evolved around them.

00:05:40.637 --> 00:05:42.356
And so who do you want to be?

00:05:42.356 --> 00:05:43.444
Do you want to be The Beatles

00:05:43.444 --> 00:05:45.611
or do you want to be a one-hit wonder?

00:05:45.611 --> 00:05:46.808
Time to decide.

00:05:46.808 --> 00:05:48.886
So the question of the
day today is, I'm curious.

00:05:48.886 --> 00:05:51.521
How have you evolved
your business with you?

00:05:51.521 --> 00:05:52.422
I'm curious,

00:05:52.422 --> 00:05:53.338
from when you started your business

00:05:53.338 --> 00:05:54.651
to where you are now.

00:05:54.651 --> 00:05:57.237
How have you grown and how
have you introduced new things

00:05:57.237 --> 00:05:58.163
into your company?

00:05:58.163 --> 00:05:59.559
I'm really curious to find out.

00:05:59.559 --> 00:06:01.276
Please leave it down the comments below.

00:06:01.276 --> 00:06:03.042
And we'll join in on the discussion.

00:06:03.042 --> 00:06:04.722
I also want to give a quick
shout to Steven Ratson.

00:06:04.722 --> 00:06:06.522
Steven, thank you so much for picking up

00:06:06.522 --> 00:06:08.412
a copy of my book, Your One Word.

00:06:08.412 --> 00:06:10.129
It really really really means a lot to me

00:06:10.129 --> 00:06:11.395
and I hope you're enjoying it.

00:06:11.395 --> 00:06:13.066
Thank you guys so much for watching.

00:06:13.066 --> 00:06:14.116
I believe in you.

00:06:14.116 --> 00:06:16.085
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:06:16.085 --> 00:06:17.671
And whatever your one word is,

00:06:17.671 --> 00:06:20.714
much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:06:20.714 --> 00:06:23.184
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:06:23.184 --> 00:06:25.817
♫ I wake up every morning

00:06:25.817 --> 00:06:29.586
♫ Entspresso keep me going

00:06:29.586 --> 00:06:30.419
Hey, Believe Nation.

00:06:30.419 --> 00:06:31.626
Thank you so much for watching.

00:06:31.626 --> 00:06:33.704
If you want to learn
more about this subject,

00:06:33.704 --> 00:06:35.311
get a little bit deeper on it.

00:06:35.311 --> 00:06:36.963
I'm going to share some extra bonus clips

00:06:36.963 --> 00:06:38.495
that I hope you'll enjoy.

00:06:38.495 --> 00:06:40.270
- Why do you still care enough to keep,

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:41.416
you're at a point in your life

00:06:41.416 --> 00:06:42.997
where you could go back.

00:06:42.997 --> 00:06:44.548
You could do your month in Vegas,

00:06:44.548 --> 00:06:46.014
and Florence Henderson could open up

00:06:46.014 --> 00:06:48.700
and you could go and hit a couple of balls

00:06:48.700 --> 00:06:50.037
and then some pinball.

00:06:50.037 --> 00:06:51.485
Why do you still care so much?

00:06:51.485 --> 00:06:53.676
- Well, I'm not comparing myself

00:06:53.676 --> 00:06:56.183
to any of these people, believe me.

00:06:56.183 --> 00:06:57.934
But you wouldn't say to Picasso.

00:06:57.934 --> 00:07:00.752
"When are you going to
put those brushes down?

00:07:00.752 --> 00:07:03.966
"Get rid of the canvas, you've done it."

00:07:03.966 --> 00:07:05.864
I'm an entertainer, first and foremost,

00:07:05.864 --> 00:07:07.101
but there's art involved here.

00:07:07.101 --> 00:07:10.150
And an artist has an
obligation to be on root.

00:07:10.150 --> 00:07:11.160
To be going somewhere.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:12.220
There's a journey involved here.

00:07:12.220 --> 00:07:14.406
And you don't know where
it is and that's the fun.

00:07:14.406 --> 00:07:16.723
So you're always going to be
seeking and looking and going

00:07:16.723 --> 00:07:18.245
and trying to challenge yourself.

00:07:18.245 --> 00:07:20.948
So without sitting around
and thinking of that a lot,

00:07:20.948 --> 00:07:22.759
it drives you and it keeps you

00:07:22.759 --> 00:07:24.670
trying to be fresh, trying to be new,

00:07:24.670 --> 00:07:26.157
trying to call on yourself.

00:07:26.157 --> 00:07:27.469
Call on yourself a little more.

00:07:27.469 --> 00:07:30.943
- And I think some of that is just,

00:07:30.943 --> 00:07:32.174
well first of all if you do very well

00:07:32.174 --> 00:07:34.528
and you make a lot of money,

00:07:34.528 --> 00:07:36.435
when you look back on your experiences

00:07:36.435 --> 00:07:39.624
and running a company
or starting a company.

00:07:39.624 --> 00:07:42.946
And there's almost a
kind of disbelief in like

00:07:42.946 --> 00:07:45.370
how did I, did I really go through that?

00:07:45.370 --> 00:07:47.214
Did I really deal with all of that pain

00:07:47.214 --> 00:07:50.188
and headache and hassle and intensity?

00:07:50.188 --> 00:07:53.017
And this is one of the reasons
why people who are founders

00:07:53.017 --> 00:07:57.184
are often so bonded together
like people who've gone to war.

00:07:58.249 --> 00:08:01.060
They'll never forget those experiences.

00:08:01.060 --> 00:08:01.893
But to get up and do that again

00:08:01.893 --> 00:08:04.476
But to get up and do that again

00:08:05.466 --> 00:08:06.812
over and over again

00:08:06.812 --> 00:08:07.714
knowing full well

00:08:07.714 --> 00:08:10.500
each time exactly what's in store for you.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:12.193
I think that is more rare

00:08:12.193 --> 00:08:13.826
I think that is more rare

00:08:13.826 --> 00:08:15.948
and it definitely requires

00:08:15.948 --> 00:08:18.382
that you're not willing
to rest on your laurels.

00:08:18.382 --> 00:08:20.029
I can't sit back and say,

00:08:20.029 --> 00:08:22.116
okay I've founded a bunch of companies.

00:08:22.116 --> 00:08:25.478
They've been tremendously successful.

00:08:25.478 --> 00:08:27.582
Therefore all my companies
are going to be successful.

00:08:27.582 --> 00:08:29.582
I have to be as paranoid

00:08:30.510 --> 00:08:33.029
and as edgy about each new company.

00:08:33.029 --> 00:08:34.620
and as edgy about each new company.

